{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be helping take care of you tonight. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi… I’ve been so nauseous all day. Started around 5 a.m. Then in the evening, I started vomiting nonstop and was sweating a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any pain with it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, a little on the right side of my belly, but not too bad. Mostly just the nausea and throwing up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We checked your blood sugar when you came in—it was very high, 529. And we found ketones, which means you were in diabetic ketoacidosis, or DKA."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh… that’s why I feel so awful. I took my Lantus the night before, but I couldn’t keep anything down today, so I didn’t take any insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Because of the DKA, you were transferred to the ICU for an insulin IV to bring your levels down safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right… I remember getting that. My stomach’s been so bad for so long. Is it just my gastroparesis flaring again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely the main trigger. Your labs showed an anion gap of 28, which confirms DKA, and your lactate was high too, at 3.7. But we’re treating that with insulin and fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood pressure was really high too, wasn’t it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it was up to the 180s. You said you take lisinopril but not metoprolol anymore?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I stopped metoprolol because it made me tired. But I still take lisinopril."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. Since you couldn’t eat at first, we gave you IV medications to control your blood pressure. Once you can eat, we’ll switch back to your usual pills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds good. I also couldn’t pee all day… that’s why they put in a catheter?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you had about 900 mL in your bladder. But no signs of infection, and you’ve been able to go on your own since then. We removed the catheter yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2198-05-05 23:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2198-05-06 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your anion gap has closed—down to 11 now—and your blood sugar is much better. The insulin drip is being stopped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2198-05-06 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! Does that mean I’m out of the woods?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2198-05-06 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The DKA is resolved, yes. But your nausea and vomiting are still ongoing. We’re continuing your usual anti-nausea meds—domperidone, Zofran, and Compazine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2198-05-06 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve tried so many things… erythromycin made me worse before. Is there anything else we can do?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2198-05-06 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The GI team is following you. They’ve suggested an outpatient EGD with possible Botox injections into your stomach to help with the gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2198-05-06 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve heard about that. Would that really help?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2198-05-06 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can help some patients reduce nausea and vomiting. It’s not permanent, but it might give you relief for a few months."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2198-05-06 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d like to try it, if my GI doctor thinks it’s right."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2198-05-06 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noticed something—we saw you putting your finger in your throat and coughing hard before vomiting. Can you tell me about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2198-05-06 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I… sometimes I feel like I need to get it over with. The nausea is so bad, I just want to vomit and be done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2198-05-06 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We understand it’s distressing. A social worker spoke with you yesterday—was that helpful?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2198-05-06 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, she was kind. I just feel stuck in this cycle. Every time I get sick, I end up here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2198-05-06 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to support you. The good news is your labs are improving. Your lactate is down to 1.0, and your kidneys are fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2198-05-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today we’re starting to advance your diet—clear liquids first, then soft foods if you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2198-05-07 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous… I haven’t kept anything down in days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2198-05-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll go slow. Small sips. And we’ll keep your anti-nausea meds going around the clock for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2198-05-07 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor? I had some apple juice and crackers… and I kept them down!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2198-05-07 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent! That’s a big step forward. Let’s try a soft meal later and see how you do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2198-05-08 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. You’ve been tolerating regular food, your blood sugars are stable on subcutaneous insulin, and your vitals are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2198-05-08 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I might be able to go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2198-05-08 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely tomorrow or the day after. We’ll make sure you’re steady on your feet and managing meals first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2198-05-08 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m on the same insulin as before—28 units Lantus at supper, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2198-05-08 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And Humalog as needed with meals, based on your blood sugar. We’ll send that home with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2198-05-08 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood pressure meds—lisinopril and metoprolol—both again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2198-05-08 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your pressure has been well-controlled since switching back to oral meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2198-05-09 07:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Last night’s blood sugar was 98, and your morning labs look great. You’re on track for discharge today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2198-05-09 07:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s such a relief. What about the EGD with Botox?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2198-05-09 07:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll set up a referral to your GI doctor. They’ll decide if it’s right for you and schedule it as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2198-05-09 07:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I start vomiting again at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2198-05-09 07:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep using your anti-nausea meds as prescribed. If you can’t keep fluids down, or your blood sugar goes very high, come back right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2198-05-09 07:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for helping me through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2198-05-10 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’ll have your discharge papers ready soon. You’re going home with the same meds, no changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2198-05-10 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up with my GI doctor?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2198-05-10 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll schedule that. And your primary care doctor too. Take care, and don’t hesitate to reach out if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2198-05-10 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just wanted to say thanks again. I feel so much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2198-05-10 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad to hear that. Keep up with your insulin and diet, and take your anti-nausea meds as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2198-05-10 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been writing down my blood sugars. Is that helpful?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2198-05-10 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. It helps you and your doctors see patterns. Keep it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2198-05-10 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. You’re cleared to go home. Rest, stay hydrated, and follow up with your GI doctor about the EGD."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2198-05-10 11:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I really appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2198-05-10 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2198-05-10 11:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—should I wear my scopolamine patch?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2198-05-10 11:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue it every 72 hours as before. It may help with nausea, especially if you’re traveling or feeling unwell."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2198-05-10 11:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2198-05-10 11:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2198-05-10 11:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m just glad to be feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2198-05-10 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad too. Take it easy and keep in touch with your team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2198-05-10 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve packed up. Ready when you are."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2198-05-10 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Discharge papers are signed. You’re officially going home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2198-05-10 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I’ll follow up with my doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2198-05-10 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Take care of yourself."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2198-05-05 23:10:00",
    "admission_end": "2198-05-10 12:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old woman with Type 1 diabetes and a history of gastroparesis was admitted for diabetic ketoacidosis triggered by severe nausea and vomiting. She presented with high blood glucose, an anion gap of 28, and ketonuria, requiring ICU-level care and an insulin infusion. Her DKA resolved within 24 hours, but nausea persisted. She was managed with IV fluids, antiemetics, and close monitoring of electrolytes and blood pressure. A urinary catheter was placed due to acute retention, with resolution within 48 hours. The GI team evaluated her for possible outpatient EGD with Botox injection for gastroparesis. She gradually advanced to a regular diet, remained stable on subcutaneous insulin, and was discharged home with no medication changes and follow-up arranged with her GI physician.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Volume depletion, unspecified",
      "Tachycardia, unspecified",
      "Retention of urine, unspecified",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Constipation, unspecified",
      "Persistent vomiting"
    ]
  }
}
